; tlswork: TLS crypto runs in the TLS process (test/amiga/tlswork.host):
; with each handshake made slow (Velox/TlsDelay) the window answers
; meanwhile; a page stopped during a handshake leaves it to finish, and
; the next TLS page waits for it; quitting during one waits for it too.
; No memory may be lost (the SSL left to the process is freed).
Echo >VELOX:r/tlswork.txt "tlswork"
; warm-up run (one-time OS allocations: fonts, CLI, AmiSSL ...)
Run >NIL: VELOX:velox https://localhost:8443/hello
Wait 15
Status >ENV:vpid COMMAND=VELOX:velox
Break $vpid C
Wait 3
Delete >NIL: ENV:vpid
Avail >NIL: FLUSH
Echo >>VELOX:r/tlswork.txt "mem_before " NOLINE
Avail >>VELOX:r/tlswork.txt TOTAL
SetEnv Velox/TlsDelay 300
Echo >VELOX:r/tlswork.start ""
VELOX:velox http://127.0.0.1:8080/index.html LOG=VELOX:r/tlswork.log
Echo >>VELOX:r/tlswork.txt "exit rc=$RC"
UnSetEnv Velox/TlsDelay
Avail >NIL: FLUSH
Echo >>VELOX:r/tlswork.txt "mem_after " NOLINE
Avail >>VELOX:r/tlswork.txt TOTAL
Echo >>VELOX:r/tlswork.txt "done"
